<title>GERMANY: Bayer deal worth $275 mln annual sales.</title>
<headline>Bayer deal worth $275 mln annual sales.</headline>
<dateline>LEVERKUSEN, Germany 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Bayer AG said on Monday that its U.S.-based joint venture with Swiss Roche Holding AG to sell over-the-counter drugs is likely to post sales of $275 million in its early years.</p>
<p>A Bayer spokesman confirmed the figure as the expected level of initial yearly revenues from the joint-venture in response to a Reuters enquiry.</p>
<p>The German chemicals and drugs giant earlier said it had signed a letter of intent to form a 50-50 joint venture with the Swiss powerhouse combining the companies' U.S. over-the-counter businesses in analgesics and women's health.</p>
<p>Both companies said the deal still needed cartel authority approval.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
